#### Challenge: Provider Deletion with Active Claims

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as Admin UI
    participant ProviderAPI as Provider Service
    participant ProviderDB as Provider DB
    participant EventBus as Azure Service Bus
    participant ClaimsAPI as Claims Service
    participant ClaimsDB as Claims DB

    Note over Admin,ClaimsDB: Saga Pattern for Distributed Transaction

    Admin->>ProviderAPI: DELETE /providers/{providerId}
    ProviderAPI->>ClaimsAPI: GET /claims?providerId={providerId}&status=Active
    ClaimsAPI->>ClaimsDB: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM Claims WHERE ProviderId=? AND Status='Active'
    ClaimsDB-->>ClaimsAPI: 150 Active Claims
    ClaimsAPI-->>ProviderAPI: 150 Active Claims Found
    ProviderAPI-->>Admin: 409 Conflict - Cannot delete provider with active claims

    Note over Admin,ClaimsDB: Alternative: Soft Delete Pattern

    Admin->>ProviderAPI: POST /providers/{providerId}/deactivate
    ProviderAPI->>ProviderDB: UPDATE Providers SET IsActive=0, DeactivatedAt=GETDATE()
    ProviderDB-->>ProviderAPI: Success
    ProviderAPI->>EventBus: Publish ProviderDeactivated Event
    ProviderAPI-->>Admin: 200 OK - Provider Deactivated

    EventBus->>ClaimsAPI: ProviderDeactivated Event
    ClaimsAPI->>ClaimsDB: UPDATE ProviderCache SET IsActive=0
    ClaimsDB-->>ClaimsAPI: Success
```

**Integrity Patterns:**

**1. Validation via API** (Synchronous)

```csharp
public class ProviderService
{
    private readonly IClaimsClient _claimsClient;
    private readonly ProviderDbContext _dbContext;

    public async Task<Result> DeleteProviderAsync(Guid providerId)
    {
        // Check referential integrity via Claims Service API
        var activeClaimsCount = await _claimsClient
            .GetActiveClaimsCountAsync(providerId);

        if (activeClaimsCount > 0)
        {
            return Result.Failure(
                $"Cannot delete provider with {activeClaimsCount} active claims");
        }

        // Safe to delete
        var provider = await _dbContext.Providers.FindAsync(providerId);
        _dbContext.Providers.Remove(provider);
        await _dbContext.SaveChangesAsync();

        return Result.Success();
    }
}
```

**2. Soft Delete Pattern** (Recommended)

```sql
-- Provider Service Database
CREATE TABLE Providers (
    ProviderId UNIQUEIDENTIFIER PRIMARY KEY,
    Name NVARCHAR(200),
    SpecialtyCode VARCHAR(10),
    IsActive BIT DEFAULT 1,
    DeactivatedAt DATETIME2 NULL,
    DeactivatedReason NVARCHAR(500) NULL
);

-- Claims Service - Validates provider is active
CREATE PROCEDURE ProcessClaim
    @ProviderId UNIQUEIDENTIFIER,
    @ClaimAmount DECIMAL(18,2)
AS
BEGIN
    -- Check provider cache (synced from Provider Service)
    IF NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM ProviderCache
        WHERE ProviderId = @ProviderId AND IsActive = 1
    )
    BEGIN
        THROW 50001, 'Provider is not active', 1;
    END;

    -- Process claim
    INSERT INTO Claims (ProviderId, Amount, Status)
    VALUES (@ProviderId, @ClaimAmount, 'Pending');
END;
```

**3. Saga Pattern** (For complex workflows)

```csharp
// Saga coordinator for provider termination workflow
public class ProviderTerminationSaga
{
    public async Task ExecuteAsync(ProviderTerminationCommand cmd)
    {
        var sagaState = new SagaState { ProviderId = cmd.ProviderId };

        try
        {
            // Step 1: Deactivate provider
            await _providerService.DeactivateProviderAsync(cmd.ProviderId);
            sagaState.ProviderDeactivated = true;

            // Step 2: Cancel pending claims
            var cancelResult = await _claimsService
                .CancelPendingClaimsAsync(cmd.ProviderId);
            sagaState.ClaimsCancelled = true;
            sagaState.CancelledClaimIds = cancelResult.ClaimIds;

            // Step 3: Reassign active claims to new provider
            await _claimsService.ReassignClaimsAsync(
                cmd.ProviderId, cmd.NewProviderId);
            sagaState.ClaimsReassigned = true;

            // Step 4: Archive provider data
            await _providerService.ArchiveProviderAsync(cmd.ProviderId);
            sagaState.Completed = true;
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            // Compensating transactions
            await CompensateAsync(sagaState);
            throw;
        }
    }

    private async Task CompensateAsync(SagaState state)
    {
        if (state.ClaimsReassigned)
        {
            await _claimsService.RollbackReassignmentAsync(state.ProviderId);
        }

        if (state.ClaimsCancelled)
        {
            await _claimsService.ReactivateClaimsAsync(state.CancelledClaimIds);
        }

        if (state.ProviderDeactivated)
        {
            await _providerService.ReactivateProviderAsync(state.ProviderId);
        }
    }
}
```

