#### Read-Heavy Workloads: Use Cached Denormalized Data

**Problem**: Claims UI displays claim with provider name (requires join across services)

```java
// ❌ Anti-Pattern: N+1 API calls
@GetMapping("/claims")
public List<ClaimSummaryResponse> getClaims() {
    List<Claim> claims = claimRepo.findAll();  // 500 claims

    return claims.stream()
        .map(claim -> {
            // API call per claim = 500 API calls!
            ProviderResponse provider = providerClient.getProvider(claim.getProviderId());
            return new ClaimSummaryResponse(claim, provider.getName());
        })
        .collect(Collectors.toList());
}
```

**Solution**: Cache provider names in Claims Service database

```sql
-- Claims Service Database - Denormalized provider cache
CREATE TABLE Claims (
    ClaimId UNIQUEIDENTIFIER PRIMARY KEY,
    ProviderId UNIQUEIDENTIFIER,
    ProviderName NVARCHAR(200),  -- Cached from Provider Service
    ProviderSpecialty VARCHAR(10), -- Cached from Provider Service
    Amount DECIMAL(18,2),
    Status VARCHAR(20),
    SubmittedAt DATETIME2
);

CREATE INDEX IX_Claims_ProviderId ON Claims(ProviderId);
CREATE INDEX IX_Claims_Status_SubmittedAt ON Claims(Status, SubmittedAt);
```

```java
// ✅ Correct: Single query with cached data
@GetMapping("/claims")
public List<ClaimSummaryResponse> getClaims() {
    // Single query returns claim + cached provider name
    return claimRepo.findAll().stream()
        .map(claim -> new ClaimSummaryResponse(
            claim.getClaimId(),
            claim.getAmount(),
            claim.getProviderName(),  // Already cached
            claim.getStatus()
        ))
        .collect(Collectors.toList());
}

// Event handler keeps cache synchronized
@EventHandler
public void handle(ProviderUpdatedEvent event) {
    claimRepo.updateProviderCache(
        event.getProviderId(),
        event.getName(),
        event.getSpecialtyCode()
    );
}
```

**Performance Impact:**
- **Before** (API composition): Sequential per-claim API calls create high cumulative latency
- **After** (cached denormalization): Single optimized query with locally cached provider data

