#### Phase 4: Migrate Existing Shared Databases

**Step 6: Use Strangler Fig Pattern for Legacy Migration**

Gradually extract services from shared database:

```text
Migration Phases for Gainwell Claims/Provider Shared Database:

Phase 1: Create Provider Service with New Database
├── Set up ProviderDB (PostgreSQL)
├── Replicate provider tables from shared database
├── Implement Provider Service API
├── Keep Provider Service reading from shared database initially
└── Duration: 2-3 sprints

Phase 2: Dual-Write Pattern
├── Provider Service writes to BOTH shared DB and ProviderDB
├── Validate data consistency between databases
├── Switch read traffic to ProviderDB (20% → 50% → 100%)
└── Duration: 2-3 sprints

Phase 3: Migrate Claims Service to Use Provider API
├── Replace Claims Service direct database queries with API calls
├── Monitor performance and adjust caching strategy
├── Update Claims Service to cache provider data locally
└── Duration: 3-4 sprints

Phase 4: Decommission Shared Provider Tables
├── Stop dual-writes (write only to ProviderDB)
├── Remove Claims Service database access to provider tables
├── Archive historical shared database data
└── Duration: 1 sprint
```

**Dual-Write Implementation:**

```csharp
// ProviderService during migration - writes to both databases
public class ProviderMigrationService
{
    private readonly ProviderDbContext _newDatabase;  // New ProviderDB
    private readonly LegacyDbContext _legacyDatabase; // Shared legacy DB
    private readonly ILogger<ProviderMigrationService> _logger;
    private readonly IConfiguration _config;

    public async Task<Result> UpdateProviderAsync(UpdateProviderCommand cmd)
    {
        var isDualWriteEnabled = _config.GetValue<bool>("Migration:DualWriteEnabled");

        try
        {
            // Write to new database (primary)
            var provider = await _newDatabase.Providers.FindAsync(cmd.ProviderId);
            provider.Name = cmd.Name;
            provider.SpecialtyCode = cmd.SpecialtyCode;
            await _newDatabase.SaveChangesAsync();

            // Write to legacy database (during migration)
            if (isDualWriteEnabled)
            {
                var legacyProvider = await _legacyDatabase.Providers
                    .FindAsync(cmd.ProviderId);
                legacyProvider.Name = cmd.Name;
                legacyProvider.SpecialtyCode = cmd.SpecialtyCode;
                await _legacyDatabase.SaveChangesAsync();
            }

            return Result.Success();
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _logger.LogError(ex, "Failed to update provider {ProviderId}", cmd.ProviderId);

            // Roll back both databases
            await RollbackAsync();
            throw;
        }
    }
}
```

